  "body": "### Summary\nAs a reader holding the iPhone in landscape with compact density, I want the section headers to line up with their rows, so that the narrower margins of #799 look right in every orientation.\n\n### Facts\nFollow-up of #804, from the round-3 review (Opus, comment on #804), which was not blocking.\n- `ListDensity.swift:117` computes the card edge as `densityCardEdge = outerMargin + safeLeading`.\n- In landscape with a 62 pt side safe area (measured through `additionalSafeAreaInsets`), the card starts at x = 62, not 72: the safe area absorbs the 10 pt margin.\n- Compact headers then sit 17 pt from the card while rows sit at 7, in RTL too.\n- Regular density is unaffected.\n\n### Scope\n- Measure the card's real edge, for example a row background's `minX` in the `densityList` coordinate space, instead of adding the two values.\n- Add a hosted test in landscape with a side safe area, in LTR and RTL, that fails today.\n\n### Acceptance criteria\n- [ ] In compact density, header text and row text sit 7 pt from the card in portrait and in landscape (safe area), LTR and RTL.\n- [ ] The new test fails at #804's head.\n- [ ] Checked on device in landscape.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_\n",
